[2026-07-29 14:56:17,226 - Orcar.agent - INFO] conclusion='<Observation>\nThe regression appears to come from model class construction rather than the display fallback itself. `Field.contribute_to_class()` unconditionally assigns `get_%s_display` onto the model when `choices` is present, so a user-defined `get_foo_bar_display()` can be overwritten during class setup in Django 2.2+. `Model._get_FIELD_display()` only returns the choice label, and `ModelBase.__new__()` / `ModelBase.add_to_class()` are the surrounding attachment points that control when this overwrite happens.\n</Observation>' bug_locations=[BugLocations(file_path='django/db/models/fields/__init__.py', class_name='Field', method_name='contribute_to_class'), BugLocations(file_path='django/db/models/base.py', class_name='ModelBase', method_name='add_to_class')]
